The Quinque viæ are five logical arguments for the existence of God summarized by the 13th-century Catholic philosopher and theologian Thomas Aquinas in his book Summa Theologica. They are:the argument from "first mover";
the argument from universal causation;
the argument from contingency;
the argument from degree;
the argument from final cause or ends.
